    {
      "attributes": {
        "description": "Items (a) and (c) of milestone 108 (analysis note 3068). (a) A read-only template collector for adcs/inventory: ldapsearch of CN=Certificate Templates,CN=Public Key Services,CN=Services,CN=Configuration,<forest root> into templates.ldif (Authenticated Users can read), following the existing collector contract (Collector, evidence, least privilege, absent markers). (c) ESC1-style template risk in the pki domain: msPKI-Certificate-Name-Flag 0x1 (ENROLLEE_SUPPLIES_SUBJECT) with a client-auth or any-purpose EKU (or no EKU), no manager approval (msPKI-Enrollment-Flag 0x2 absent), no authorized signatures required, and enrollment rights for broad groups (from nTSecurityDescriptor); the showcase fixture's CIAM-WebServer sets name flag 1. Findings go to the template's renewal owner as data. Research current ESC definitions (SpecterOps Certified Pre-Owned and later ESC numbering) and the template attribute forms first (Codex, read-only). Design to the master before coding if it changes what the record holds (e.g. recording enrollment rights). Items (b) CRL/OCSP observation, (d) exporter acceptance and (e) other CAs stay for later tasks.",
        "flows": [
          "PKI Authorities & Issued-Certificate Reconciliation",
          "AD CS Inventory Import"
        ],
        "name": "AD CS certificate-template collector and ESC1-style template risk",
        "parent": {
